---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Example from '../../components/Example.astro';
import CodeViewer from '../../components/CodeViewer.astro';
const sections=[{id:'finishes',title:'Six finishes'},{id:'install',title:'Installation'},{id:'inheritance',title:'Inheritance'},{id:'motion',title:'Press and return'},{id:'configuration',title:'Numeric values'},{id:'limits',title:'Preferences and limits'}];
const materials=[['default','Follow the surrounding material.'],['solid','Opaque semantic colour.'],['glass','Frosted, translucent colour.'],['veil','Diffused perimeter colour.'],['soft','Paired raised and inset shadows.'],['liquid','Reflective glass with fluid press feedback.']];
const install=`<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-material="soft" data-button-material="liquid" data-motion="subtle">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Independent button materials</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reva.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reva.soft.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="reva.button-materials.css">
</head>
<body>
  <article class="card"><h1>Your project</h1><button type="button">Save changes</button></article>
</body>
</html>`;
const inheritance=`<section data-material="soft" data-button-material="liquid" class="stack">
  <article class="card"><h3>Soft card, liquid actions</h3><div class="row">
    <button type="button">Continue</button>
    <button type="button" data-button-material="solid">Solid exception</button>
    <button type="button" data-button-material="default">Follow Soft UI</button>
  </div></article>
  <section data-button-material="default" data-material="glass">
    <button type="button">Follow Glass</button>
    <button type="button" data-button-material="liquid">Liquid again</button>
  </section>
</section>`;
const targets=`<section data-button-material="liquid" class="row">
  <button type="button">Native button</button>
  <input type="button" value="Native input action">
  <a class="button" href="#install">Button link</a>
  <a class="scroll-top" href="#page-top">Back to top</a>
</section>`;
---
<DocsLayout title="Button materials" active="button-materials" sections={sections}>
<p class="doc-kicker">OPTIONAL ACTION MATERIAL / 1.2 DEVELOPMENT PREVIEW</p><h1>Button materials</h1>
<p class="doc-lead">Choose a finish for actions while cards, menus and text fields keep their own material. Configure the page once, then override only exceptions.</p>
<p class="doc-note">This addition is available in the development preview and planned for 1.2.0. The 1.1.0 GitHub archives and current npm package do not include it.</p>
<section id="finishes"><h2>Six finishes, one attribute</h2><p>These examples follow this page’s theme and palette. Use Customize → Surfaces → Button material to try the setting across documentation and demos.</p>
<div class="grid">{materials.map(([value,description])=><section class="button-stage" data-button-material={value} aria-label={`${value} button material`}><h3><code>{value}</code></h3><p>{description}</p><div class="row"><button type="button">Continue</button><button type="button" class="secondary">Preview</button></div></section>)}</div>
</section>
<section id="install"><h2>Load the optional module</h2><p>Load <code>reva.button-materials.css</code> after the complete core. It includes all five explicit finishes; load the general Glass, Veil or Soft UI extensions only when you also need those materials on other surfaces. Omitted or <code>default</code> button material preserves the surrounding material.</p><CodeViewer id="button-material-install" code={install}/>
<p>For scoped use, load <code>reva.scoped.css</code> and <code>reva.button-materials.scoped.css</code>, and configure <code>data-button-material</code> on <code>.reva</code> or within it. Modular applications load tokens, base and this extension, plus any structural modules used by their markup.</p></section>
<Example id="inheritance" title="Inherited choices and local resets" description="An explicit button finish applies through general material boundaries. Default stops that finish and follows the general material at each action; a new local choice can resume it." html={inheritance}/>
<Example id="action-targets" title="The same finish on every action type" description="Native button and button/submit/reset inputs, .button links and .scroll-top actions share the material. Text fields, switches, checkboxes, cards and ordinary links keep their own styles." html={targets}/>
<section id="motion"><h2>Press and return</h2><p>Liquid uses reflective rims, tint and backdrop blur to suggest a glass surface. Pressing gently expands it; release returns it with elastic easing. This is a CSS simulation, with a fixed highlight rather than a reflection that tracks your finger.</p>
<div class="grid" data-button-material="liquid">{['none','subtle','expressive'].map(motion=><section class="button-stage" data-motion={motion}><h3>{motion}</h3><button type="button">Press and release</button></section>)}</div>
<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Liquid button motion levels" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Motion</th><th scope="col">Press</th><th scope="col">Return</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">none</th><td>Immediate highlight; no expansion</td><td>Immediate</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">subtle</th><td>1.025 × 1.015 scale; 140ms</td><td>280ms elastic easing</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">expressive</th><td>1.045 × 1.02 scale; 240ms</td><td>480ms elastic easing</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Reduced motion removes expansion and transitions. Expansion uses transforms, so it does not reflow neighbouring content; leave enough surrounding space and avoid clipping the button’s rim or focus outline. Press feedback follows native <code>:active</code>. Keyboard activation and focus remain native; browsers that do not expose active state during a keyboard press activate the action without the expansion.</p></section>
<section id="configuration"><h2>Numeric customization</h2><CodeViewer id="liquid-numeric" lang="css" code={'html {\n  --re-liquid-scale-x: 1.035;\n  --re-liquid-scale-y: 1.015;\n  --re-liquid-blur: 10px;\n  --re-liquid-opacity: 98%;\n}'}/><p>Scale values are positive numbers, blur is a nonnegative length and opacity is a percentage. Place overrides on the same configured boundary or on an action. A local motion preset installs its own scale defaults. Motion none and reduced motion suppress expansion even with custom scale values. Lower backing opacity requires reviewing text contrast over the actual background.</p></section>
<section id="limits"><h2>Preferences and limits</h2><ul>
<li>Semantic variants keep their meaning and colours. Shape, size, density, borders and depth remain separate settings. Outline and ghost actions retain transparent backing and their own borders; liquid motion can still apply.</li>
<li>Increased contrast and reduced transparency simplify decorative paint and use opaque backing. Explicit More Contrast disables blur and decoration. Forced colours and print use plain accessible paint and remove movement.</li>
<li>Browsers without backdrop filtering retain opaque action colours. Browsers without <code>linear()</code> easing use the cubic Bézier fallback.</li>
<li>Native focus outlines and activation remain intact. Disabled controls do not expand; <code>aria-disabled</code> describes state but application code must prevent an unavailable link or action from activating.</li>
<li>Liquid adds no optical refraction, finger tracking, haptics or framework JavaScript. RevaCSS does not reproduce Apple’s native rendering engine.</li>
</ul><p>Standards: <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-cascade-6/#scoped-rules">CSS scopes and cascade</a>, <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-easing-2/">CSS easing</a> and <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#the-active-pseudo">native active state</a>.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
<style>.button-stage { padding:1.5rem; border:1px solid var(--re-line); border-radius:var(--re-radius); background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 0% 0%,color-mix(in srgb,var(--re-primary) 12%,transparent),transparent 70%); } .button-stage .row { gap:1.25rem; } @media print { .button-stage { background:none; } }</style>
